%description:

Tcp.abortOnDataAfterClose:rfc -- after a CLOSE, host1 still takes the data of its peer.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "model the full close of Linux close(): a CLOSE without halfClose also
shuts the receive side down, and new data after it resets the connection (RFC 1122 section
4.2.2.13); false: RFC 9293 CLOSE, after which the application may still receive".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and linux (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::process_CLOSE() shuts the receive side down at a CLOSE without halfClose, with
true; then TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th() answers new data in FIN_WAIT_1 or
FIN_WAIT_2 with a RST. This test separates "rfc" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, whose TcpTestApp connects to host2 at 0.1 s and closes the connection
at 0.5 s (a CLOSE without halfClose); the TcpTestApp of host2 does not close, and sends 1000
bytes at 0.7 s, while host1 is in FIN_WAIT_2. Observation: level 1, host1 acknowledges the 1000 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.abortOnDataAfterClose
%# class: rfc
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.abortOnDataAfterClose
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAbortOnDataAfterCloseRfc")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().bind(1000); app.socket().listen(); })
                 .describe("host2 listens"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000); })
                 .describe("host1 connects to host2"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .capture("peerIsn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().close(); })
                 .describe("host1 closes the connection"))
        .act(action().at(0.7).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.sendData(app.accepted(0), 1000); })
                 .describe("host2 sends 1000 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {peerIsn} + 1001 && tcp.rstBit == false")
             .describe("the ACK of the 1000 bytes")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAbortOnDataAfterCloseRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.abortOnDataAfterClose = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAbortOnDataAfterCloseRfc: PASS
